	(text "24 V INPUT / TVS / BRANCH FUSES / 12 V AUX BUCK"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid ded084e6-35d1-4cf4-9ce1-d0c0b47b8dae)
	)
	(text "J901 XT60PW-M: pin 1 = GND (-), pin 2 = +24V (+), per KiCad AMASS footprint silkscreen.\nPolarity is protected only by the keyed connector; there is no electronic reverse protection.\nBuild the PSU cable once, check polarity with a meter, keep the female (socket) on the PSU side."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid b81cdfcd-6c93-4b4d-a77d-f243d9eb6a83)
	)
	(text "External PSU: 24.0 V set point, <=25 V. D901 SMBJ26CA: 26 V standoff, 42.1 V clamp at 14.3 A (25 C).\nAL8853 VIN pins now use 12 V aux; their power inductors still use 24 V.\nF902 10 A loads; LED channels fused individually on sheet 07 (F711 6.3 A, F721 3 A); F904 2 A aux. PSU must protect the unfused XT60/TVS input segment."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 83.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid 338c23fd-a4ac-46f5-ab95-60b128b3e5c5)
	)
	(text "12 V AUX: two fans, UCC27524A, TPS54202 and both AL8853 VIN pins. LMR16020, ~526 kHz (RT 47k), 22 uH.\nVout = 0.75 x (1 + 150k/10k) = 12.00 V; 0.1% divider, static range 11.74..12.26 V. Budget 1.2 A.\nEN divider 560k/47k retained. C909 100u polymer + C910 22u ceramic; verify startup/load steps and thermal vias.\nF904 and downstream fuses do not qualify fault clearing; test against the actual PSU and cables."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 172.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid a13ce5ee-bd19-41c1-9f3b-1d3e5df91115)
	)
